1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:08,000
[A mother in Karauli, speaking Braj]
“My child is ten… how do I teach him?”

2
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:13,330
I'm Santram, from a village in Rajasthan.

3
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:18,200
I grew up memorising books; it took
me thirty years to learn to ask why.

4
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:20,420
Parents here still say,
“padho, padho” (study!),

5
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:23,430
but nobody shows them how
to make a child curious.

6
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:26,700
In rural government schools,
fewer than one in four

7
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:29,630
Class 3 children can read a Class 2 story.

8
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:32,470
Children here don't lack talent.

9
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:35,280
They lack exposure:
someone to ask them why.

10
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,930
So I built Marg, which means path.

11
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:41,560
Not a tutor, and not
screen time for children.

12
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:44,390
It equips the people
around a child to teach

13
00:00:44,410 --> 00:00:45,790
the way children learn best:

14
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:49,080
through play, talk, and
the world around them.

15
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:52,380
The world is the curriculum;
Marg is the guide.

16
00:00:52,530 --> 00:00:53,680
Does it work?

17
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:56,160
Here's a real field test, in my village.

18
00:01:40,330 --> 00:01:46,980
Eight real people tried it, unscripted.
Thirty-one things broke, and I fixed every one the same day.

19
00:01:49,330 --> 00:01:52,310
A real voice note on the
live demo: transcribed,

20
00:01:52,330 --> 00:01:54,760
checked by Llama Guard and Muse Spark,

21
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:56,800
answered in Braj, and checked again.

22
00:01:57,780 --> 00:02:01,140
Here, Llama Guard is off.
Muse Spark checks instead,

23
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:03,250
and nothing goes out unchecked.

24
00:02:04,310 --> 00:02:06,770
Muse Spark Open, an open-weights model,

25
00:02:06,790 --> 00:02:08,500
reflects on the child.

26
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:11,060
Underneath, a hexagonal architecture:

27
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,960
every model sits behind a port,

28
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:15,280
so every test runs without a live model.

29
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:18,690
Six Meta models, each with one job,

30
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:21,750
at about three cents a
family a day in model calls.

31
00:02:21,770 --> 00:02:25,070
A real system doesn't need
the most expensive model.

32
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:27,630
It needs the right model for each job.

33
00:02:28,910 --> 00:02:31,850
Nine in ten rural teenagers
have a smartphone at home:

34
00:02:31,870 --> 00:02:35,040
that's Marg's reach, with
no app, just a voice note.

35
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:37,700
One parent, one child, every day.

36
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:39,710
One teacher, a whole class.

37
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:44,170
250 million young children are at
risk of missing their potential.

38
00:02:44,190 --> 00:02:46,730
Nothing in Marg is only for my village.

39
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:47,770
Thank you.

